WEBVTT

01:35.290 --> 01:37.380
Today marks the end of Golden Week.

01:38.040 --> 01:43.830
Once school starts back up,
it'll be harder to visit haunts on consecutive days.

01:44.540 --> 01:45.750
So let's give this one 100%.

01:46.130 --> 01:46.750
Right.

01:47.210 --> 01:51.830
This building falls on a dragon vein
that flows from Nikko Toshogu Shrine to Edo Castle,

01:52.130 --> 01:55.170
and is built upon a point
where spiritual energy naturally pools.

01:56.420 --> 01:57.630
It's an old love hotel.

01:59.250 --> 02:01.830
N-not a place we should bring a kid...

02:02.500 --> 02:06.540
I've never been to a love hotel, abandoned or otherwise.

02:06.790 --> 02:09.040
Yeah. I know.

02:09.040 --> 02:10.290
You would.

02:11.250 --> 02:12.750
Neither have I.

02:15.460 --> 02:17.670
But you'll fix that, right, Kei-kun?

02:15.630 --> 02:19.080
<b>YOU'LL FIX THAT, RIGHT, KEI-KUN?</b>

02:15.630 --> 02:19.080
<b>YOU'LL FIX THAT, RIGHT, KEI-KUN?</b>

02:15.630 --> 02:19.080
<b>YOU'LL FIX THAT, RIGHT, KEI-KUN?</b>

02:15.630 --> 02:19.080
<b>YOU'LL FIX THAT, RIGHT, KEI-KUN?</b>

02:20.830 --> 02:27.790
Th-that's kinda a big deal, s-so might we
broach this topic of conversation at another time?

02:28.000 --> 02:30.040
Sure. Don't forget.

02:30.250 --> 02:31.130
Keitaro.

02:31.960 --> 02:34.710
Don't know what you guys are talking about,
but can we get back to it?

02:34.710 --> 02:36.040
Y-yeah!

02:36.420 --> 02:40.420
Stories say the ghosts of women
haunt the halls of this love hotel.

02:41.250 --> 02:44.290
It was once owned by a criminal enterprise.

02:44.290 --> 02:49.380
Their leaders would drag women here,
have their way with them, then kill them.

02:50.170 --> 02:55.920
His victims were drugged, then died either from
overdose or the violence inflicted on them.

02:56.830 --> 03:03.170
Now, their spirits are bound to the hotel,
wandering the halls in a desperate attempt to escape.

03:03.750 --> 03:09.420
That's the story I found online,
but from what I've seen, it seems mostly true.

03:10.670 --> 03:13.130
But that's just what the public knows.

03:14.420 --> 03:16.040
There's one more phenomenon going on inside.

03:16.330 --> 03:18.040
I figured it out while observing the ghosts.

03:19.210 --> 03:26.210
Though they're all looking for the exit,
they all disappear before passing through it.

03:27.080 --> 03:30.750
The location they disappear in is likely the location
where they lost consciousness.

03:31.130 --> 03:34.710
And after they disappear, their location seems to reset.

03:35.170 --> 03:36.210
Reset?

03:36.920 --> 03:42.290
Uh-huh. I'm guessing the victims
were all abused in different rooms.

03:42.790 --> 03:47.290
But their terror and desperation
to escape have all merged together,

03:47.460 --> 03:51.000
creating a room that doesn't exist
that they now all try to escape.

03:51.540 --> 03:56.330
That's the phenomenon
the public doesn't know about: the "secret room."

03:57.170 --> 03:59.830
Normally, there's no way to get in there.

04:00.460 --> 04:01.920
And that's where I hid our Graduate.

04:01.920 --> 04:02.920
Huh?!

04:02.920 --> 04:04.880
Wh-why there?!

04:04.880 --> 04:07.420
Wait, you said "normally," right?

04:07.920 --> 04:12.170
Uh-huh. I figured out how to get in
by observing the ghosts.

04:12.920 --> 04:16.000
The wandering ghosts are all trying to escape that room.

04:16.460 --> 04:20.170
They follow a path through certain room numbers.

04:20.630 --> 04:26.710
By reversing the order they travel,
we get a route that leads us straight to the secret room.

04:28.500 --> 04:31.960
The Graduate's hidden in the bathroom
of that secret room,

04:31.960 --> 04:34.920
but I ran into an issue when I went to get her last time.

04:35.710 --> 04:39.540
I got to the secret room,
but every time I went through the door...

04:40.250 --> 04:43.830
I ended up back at the entrance to the hotel.
I couldn't get to her at all.

04:44.000 --> 04:44.750
What?

04:45.250 --> 04:48.250
The courtesan Graduate has manipulated the room

04:48.250 --> 04:53.250
to only admit those she "fancies,"
turning it into her private pleasure district.

04:55.250 --> 04:58.170
And she really, really doesn’t like me.

04:59.000 --> 05:06.460
But she'll probably invite you right in, Keitaro,
especially 'cause you're a man.

05:06.670 --> 05:08.250
So I'm gonna need your help.

05:12.880 --> 05:13.830
Okay.

05:14.130 --> 05:18.330
I'll send you the instructions for getting
to the secret room. Memorize them good.

05:18.460 --> 05:19.540
Got it.

05:20.000 --> 05:21.250
<b>YAYOI-CHAN</b>

05:20.000 --> 05:21.250
<b>HOW TO GET TO THE SECRET ROOM</b>

05:20.000 --> 05:21.250
<b>Ignore all other ghosts until you see one with waist-length hair.</b>

05:20.000 --> 05:21.250
<b>1. Before it gets to Room 203, change the room number to 413.</b>

05:20.000 --> 05:21.250
<b>2. Close the door to Room 304.</b>

05:20.000 --> 05:21.250
<b>3. Change the number on Room 413 to 203 and leave the door open.</b>

05:21.420 --> 05:22.920
As always, you'll need these.

05:23.290 --> 05:27.000
If things get gnarly, use these to stay safe.

05:27.330 --> 05:29.710
Wait, is this the Martyr?!

05:30.170 --> 05:32.290
And this is from Castle H...

05:32.670 --> 05:34.920
Okay, let's go.

05:50.500 --> 05:52.420
Wait, where'd they go?

05:57.170 --> 05:58.920
Wh-what the hell?

05:59.290 --> 06:01.500
Did everything just randomly change on me?!

06:02.540 --> 06:08.130
No, I must've wandered out of my world...
and into the spirit world.

06:09.000 --> 06:10.210
I gotta get out of here.

06:10.460 --> 06:14.000
But what do I do? I don't even know how...

06:14.210 --> 06:16.540
Stop it. Don't give up!

06:16.540 --> 06:17.790
I have to think!

06:20.540 --> 06:21.380
Is this a moat?

06:22.790 --> 06:24.920
...turning it into her private pleasure district.

06:25.880 --> 06:30.710
Right... Back in the Edo period,
the pleasure district was surrounded by a moat.

06:31.960 --> 06:35.170
Did the Graduate do this, then?

06:35.920 --> 06:40.960
If she did, then strengthening the seal on her
should put an end to it!

06:44.420 --> 06:45.380
Keitaro...

06:45.920 --> 06:47.040
He's gone!

06:52.170 --> 06:53.540
Is that his voice?

06:54.130 --> 06:55.380
It sounds like him.

06:57.080 --> 06:59.920
Eiko, can you see him on the GPS?

07:00.670 --> 07:01.170
I'll check!

07:07.210 --> 07:08.130
Found him!

07:09.080 --> 07:10.880
He's right at the entrance!

07:12.040 --> 07:14.080
Considering he disappeared,

07:14.380 --> 07:16.630
<b>REAL WORLD</b>

07:14.830 --> 07:19.920
Keitaro must be in the same coordinates,
but in the spirit world.

07:16.630 --> 07:20.630
<b>SPIRIT WORLD</b>

07:27.830 --> 07:29.290
A ghost...

07:29.290 --> 07:31.630
Yayoi-chan, Kei-kun's on the move!

07:32.710 --> 07:36.540
Let's follow him and find the secret room.

07:36.540 --> 07:37.290
Okay.

07:46.790 --> 07:49.540
1. Before it gets to Room 203,

07:47.750 --> 07:50.170
<b>1. Before it gets to Room 203,</b>

07:47.750 --> 07:50.170
<b>change the room number to 413 and open the door.</b>

07:49.540 --> 07:53.290
change the room number to 413 and open the door.

07:53.500 --> 07:57.080
Change the number, open the door...

08:00.040 --> 08:01.580
I followed her directions.

08:07.790 --> 08:09.790
Maybe it's because I'm in the spirit world...

08:10.960 --> 08:12.380
but I can see them now.

08:13.330 --> 08:15.420
Now, her path should change...

08:46.880 --> 08:48.710
Wh-what are those things?!

08:49.170 --> 08:52.710
I don't sense anything from them,
but I can tell they're bad news just from looking at them!

08:53.500 --> 08:57.710
No, hold on. They've got to be part of what
leads us to the secret room.

08:58.250 --> 09:01.330
I have to run ahead of her and follow the next steps.

09:03.540 --> 09:06.830
2. Close the door to Room 304.

09:04.080 --> 09:06.880
<b>2. Close the door to Room 304.</b>

09:07.630 --> 09:10.000
Close the door to room 304...

09:25.250 --> 09:26.420
HOT!

09:37.830 --> 09:39.630
It's coming this way.

09:40.670 --> 09:42.210
But it's not coming after me.

09:42.500 --> 09:44.790
Remember, you're leading it somewhere!

09:46.040 --> 09:49.000
3. Change the number on Room 413 to 203

09:46.250 --> 09:47.960
<b>3. Change the number on Room 413</b>

09:46.250 --> 09:47.960
<b>to 203 and leave the door open.</b>

09:49.000 --> 09:52.080
and leave the door open.

10:41.580 --> 10:43.170
I've gotta go after her.

10:47.500 --> 10:50.710
It's so hard to breathe. The air feels so heavy.

10:56.790 --> 10:59.540
That must be the secret room.

11:00.080 --> 11:02.420
I made it!

11:11.130 --> 11:14.790
Wh-what the...? What's happening?

11:16.210 --> 11:18.580
I'm saved.

11:18.790 --> 11:21.080
I'm seeing myself.

11:21.790 --> 11:23.420
Wait, was I...

11:23.960 --> 11:25.880
...switched with her?

11:31.170 --> 11:32.250
I'm back!

11:32.670 --> 11:33.630
Wait!

11:38.170 --> 11:39.710
Switch with me...

12:00.670 --> 12:02.880
Someone's in there.

12:05.290 --> 12:06.210
Help...

12:16.790 --> 12:17.670
Eiko!

12:18.080 --> 12:19.540
Kei-kun?!

12:21.960 --> 12:24.080
How did you end up here? Where's Yayoi-chan?

12:24.080 --> 12:26.420
I don't know, she only took me...

12:29.210 --> 12:32.250
I knew you'd come save me.

12:42.920 --> 12:46.040
Thank you. I'm so happy you came.

12:46.540 --> 12:49.630
When we get home, I'll give you a nice, big reward.

12:49.920 --> 12:54.210
So could you hurry up and get these ropes off me?

12:54.670 --> 12:56.790
What did she just say?

12:57.710 --> 12:59.500
Is she...

13:02.170 --> 13:04.500
...really Eiko?

13:18.580 --> 13:21.080
She's not Eiko!

13:21.380 --> 13:23.540
C'mon, hurry.

13:23.790 --> 13:25.540
She's the Graduate!

13:25.920 --> 13:28.540
And she's trying to get me to release her!

13:31.080 --> 13:32.040
No.

13:32.210 --> 13:34.960
Aww, why not, Kei-kun?

13:36.080 --> 13:38.330
Because you're a bad actress!

13:40.750 --> 13:44.500
I'm gonna squeeze your balls till they explode,
you little bitch.

13:47.000 --> 13:50.880
Leave this room and you'll never go back.

13:52.960 --> 13:56.080
I'll burn it all down and trap you here forever.

13:56.210 --> 14:00.170
You'll be stuck here with me till the end of time.

14:00.880 --> 14:03.750
But you don't want that. You wanna get outta here.

14:04.330 --> 14:06.080
Want me to help?

14:06.790 --> 14:10.960
Then get this pesky rope off me, now!

14:12.170 --> 14:16.290
Y'know, I like men who finish the job quick.

14:26.710 --> 14:29.040
If things get gnarly, use these to stay safe.

14:32.710 --> 14:33.500
Ow!

14:33.960 --> 14:37.750
Aww, honey, you're no fun.

14:39.710 --> 14:45.210
Boys who don't listen get punished 'round here.

14:54.330 --> 14:57.420
You'll be like this soon, too!

15:10.500 --> 15:12.960
Wh-what's happening to me?

15:13.080 --> 15:17.210
It's already started. Won't be long now.

15:18.170 --> 15:21.170
I'm gonna be like that?

15:23.130 --> 15:25.000
Want it to go away?

15:25.000 --> 15:28.630
Want to do something
before this room goes up in flames?

15:28.630 --> 15:30.580
Then c'mon...

15:31.000 --> 15:35.460
If you don't hurry up, we'll both be goners.

15:40.040 --> 15:41.380
The spirit stopped here.

15:43.460 --> 15:44.920
I hear Keitaro.

15:47.580 --> 15:50.250
Kei-kun is in there.

15:53.460 --> 15:55.500
C'mon, hurry.

15:56.130 --> 15:58.080
O-okay!

15:59.170 --> 16:01.000
There's a good boy.

16:01.000 --> 16:04.170
You should've just done this from the beginning.

16:07.630 --> 16:12.130
WHAT THE FUCK ARE YOU DOING, ASSHOLE?!

16:12.130 --> 16:13.420
Her hand stopped me!

16:15.830 --> 16:20.330
If I strengthen her seal,
everything that's her doing will disappear!

16:20.630 --> 16:21.630
Just a little more!

16:29.790 --> 16:31.830
Switch with me!

16:32.130 --> 16:34.330
Please, not now!

16:36.420 --> 16:38.750
Please, not now!

16:53.670 --> 16:54.630
Just in case.

16:57.330 --> 16:58.380
It's gone!

17:01.460 --> 17:02.460
It's gone!

17:05.580 --> 17:06.790
That was Kei-kun.

17:15.040 --> 17:17.330
Kei-kun? Is this you?

17:23.920 --> 17:26.790
Please, Kei-kun, don't do this.

17:27.040 --> 17:29.630
We could do something so much more fun.

17:31.000 --> 17:31.960
Please?

17:34.000 --> 17:35.790
DON'T INSULT EIKO LIKE THIS!

17:36.000 --> 17:38.380
SHE'S NOT A SLUT LIKE YOU!

17:38.540 --> 17:41.750
A slut? A slut?!

17:41.880 --> 17:46.830
DO YOU HAVE ANY IDEA WHO YOU'RE INSULTING?!

17:53.080 --> 17:54.080
Kei-kun!

18:10.210 --> 18:11.210
Kei-kun!
Keitaro!<b></b>

18:11.750 --> 18:14.380
Eiko? Yayoi-chan?

18:16.960 --> 18:17.960
I'm back!

18:18.170 --> 18:20.790
A-are you okay?! You're hurt!

18:20.790 --> 18:25.130
I'm fine. It's not as bad as it looks.

18:26.710 --> 18:28.000
You've got her.

18:28.830 --> 18:31.130
You did a great job, all by yourself, too.

18:32.790 --> 18:34.920
I had some help in the end.

18:35.580 --> 18:37.710
Things weren't looking good for me,

18:38.040 --> 18:41.290
but Eiko's helping hand literally saved me.

18:43.290 --> 18:45.380
I-I had no idea what I was doing.

18:45.630 --> 18:47.960
The curse must've connected us or something.

18:47.960 --> 18:51.130
I'm just glad you're okay.

18:51.580 --> 18:55.710
Eiko... Thanks. I owe you.

18:57.420 --> 18:58.130
Sure.

18:59.210 --> 19:02.960
Okay, we've got Keitaro back and the doll we came for.

19:02.960 --> 19:04.210
Let's head out.

19:04.790 --> 19:05.710
Roger that!

19:09.670 --> 19:12.040
I learned in history class that courtesans

19:12.330 --> 19:13.960
were pretty talented women.

19:14.670 --> 19:16.540
I'm sure you were one of them, too.

19:17.250 --> 19:21.580
But my girlfriend's pretty damn incredible.

19:23.580 --> 19:24.580
With that out of the way,

19:25.290 --> 19:26.580
let's get to business.

19:26.670 --> 19:27.920
I forgot.

19:28.080 --> 19:29.710
All that work,

19:29.710 --> 19:31.830
but it wasn't even the main thing we were after...

19:31.830 --> 19:34.960
We're headed off to an S-Rank haunt,

19:34.960 --> 19:36.420
the Old I Watergate.

19:36.830 --> 19:38.040
Let's ghoooo...

19:38.040 --> 19:39.080
...ooost!

19:39.080 --> 19:39.960
Wait a sec!

19:39.960 --> 19:41.080
We're not waiting!

19:41.080 --> 19:41.790
Nope!

19:41.790 --> 19:43.290
Oh, come on!

19:44.710 --> 19:48.130
Is it okay to leave the rest of the hotel's ghosts there?

19:48.130 --> 19:50.670
They seemed like they wanted to get out of there,

19:50.670 --> 19:54.710
and they attacked me,
so they could go after someone else...

19:54.960 --> 19:56.330
It's totally okay.

19:56.790 --> 20:00.750
They only attacked us 'cause we messed with them.

20:02.290 --> 20:05.170
A while back, when I first found the secret room,

20:05.960 --> 20:11.080
I also found some ghosts
that harbored particularly strong grudges.

20:11.420 --> 20:16.960
They were torturing the gang members
who had killed them... and locking them in a closet.

20:19.960 --> 20:23.210
One they're all dead, the ghosts should pass on.

20:23.670 --> 20:27.000
I'm fine with that. It's what they deserve.

20:27.670 --> 20:31.830
But you said they attacked you. What'd they do to you?

20:33.080 --> 20:38.960
Well, it's gonna sound crazy,
but one of them tried to switch places with me.

20:39.380 --> 20:40.580
Switch places with you?

20:40.580 --> 20:43.210
Yeah, like, literally.

20:43.880 --> 20:51.500
The second it touched me, the spirit was in my body,
and I'd turned into the spirit.

20:52.330 --> 20:57.000
But when I knocked its hand away,
I went back to normal.

20:57.630 --> 21:01.880
Keitaro, do you remember what day it was we met?

21:02.330 --> 21:05.130
Huh? April 1st, why?

21:05.130 --> 21:08.880
That's right. And that means you're you and not a ghost.

21:08.880 --> 21:09.540
Wha-?!

21:10.040 --> 21:14.880
Oh, God. The spirit could've been
in control of him this whole time.

21:15.080 --> 21:21.130
Uh-huh. That's why I had to check
if our memories matched up.

21:21.670 --> 21:24.130
And if we'd switched, I would've been dead.

21:24.580 --> 21:28.040
Now that I'm thinking it over,
that whole situation was really messed up...

21:28.330 --> 21:32.920
That spirit would be pretending to be me,
acting as if nothing was wrong...

21:33.380 --> 21:38.000
That reminds me of a similar story I read online.

21:38.790 --> 21:45.170
A man and his son were spending the night in their car
after it broke down on a mountain road.

21:45.460 --> 21:51.000
The father was keeping watch on his son while he slept,
and was just about to pass out,

21:52.250 --> 21:54.630
when he spotted something coming towards them.

22:01.170 --> 22:04.540
He was too shocked to react or even scream.

22:05.500 --> 22:10.630
The white creature did nothing to them,
just went past the car...

22:11.710 --> 22:15.210
But just when the man thought they were safe...

22:15.670 --> 22:17.420
He looked over at his son.

22:21.580 --> 22:24.080
"Get the hell away from my son!"

22:24.710 --> 22:26.290
The moment he yelled out...

22:29.710 --> 22:34.960
"I'm in! I'm in! I'm in! I'm in!"

22:35.290 --> 22:39.380
He rushed down the mountain
to bring his son to a temple,

22:39.920 --> 22:42.330
but the priest said if 49 days passed
and nothing changed,

22:42.330 --> 22:45.080
he would be stuck like that forever.

22:42.330 --> 22:46.170
I'm in! I'm in! I'm in! I'm in!

22:47.920 --> 22:51.580
It kind of reminds me
of how you describe getting "switched."

22:52.080 --> 22:56.500
I remember Keitaro's grandma
saying something similar about her dolls, too.

22:56.920 --> 22:59.750
Must be something that can happen, then.

23:00.380 --> 23:04.460
Now that we know about it, though,
we can prepare to counter it.

23:04.580 --> 23:05.380
Uh-huh.

23:06.080 --> 23:12.500
Spirits and humans, switching... That means evil spirits
could walk amongst us, pretending to be human.

23:14.170 --> 23:18.670
So... how would you tell the difference?

23:22.460 --> 23:30.330
Strangers search for a stolen relic,
unbeknownst to Yayoi and the team.

23:31.330 --> 23:35.040
Both head to the Old I Watergate
to fulfill their own purposes.

23:35.790 --> 23:40.540
Waiting for them there is a forlorn boy,
casting a shadow in the twilight.
